<section>
    <h3>One file per test, wherever you want it</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-php" data-trim data-line-numbers="1-5|1|2|3|5">
#[UseRecord]                             // ClassName/methodName.har, next to the test
#[UseRecord('fixtures/random.har')]      // relative to the directory of the test
#[UseRecord('/var/fixtures/random.har')] // absolute

// with a data provider: testRandom@dataSetName.har
    </code></pre>
    <ul style="font-size: 0.65em;">
        <li class="fragment">On the class: applies to every test, the attribute on the method wins</li>
        <li class="fragment">With <code>http-recorder-directory</code>: every path starts from that directory, and the default path follows the namespace of the test</li>
    </ul>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>A few variants, quickly.</p>
        <p>[click] By default, the file is named after the class and the method, next to the test.</p>
        <p>[click] You can give the attribute a file name, relative to the directory of the test…</p>
        <p>[click] … or an absolute path.</p>
        <p>[click] With a data provider, you get one file per data set: testRandom@dataSetName.har.</p>
        <p>[click] You can put the attribute on the class, and the one on the method wins.</p>
        <p>[click] And with http-recorder-directory, every path starts from that directory, and the default path follows the namespace of the test, so two classes with the same name don't collide.</p>
        <p>And if you don't use PHPUnit, you can build the client by hand with a RecorderConfiguration.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
